      children: "The mesh pattern excels in highly distributed, large-scale systems where centralization would create bottlenecks. Since agents communicate directly, latency is minimized-no extra hop through a coordinator. The system is inherently resilient: failure of any single agent only affects requests to that specific agent, not the entire system. And scaling is granular: each agent type can be independently provisioned based on its specific load patterns."
